ity in Washington, DC, examined; details given of the arrest of Eisa al-Hindi, the man accused of directing the surveillance of financial institutions in the US.  [Capitol Hill resident Anne O'ROURKE&#134;, worker Mary Louise FAUNCE&#134;- react to the security.]  [Capitol Police Chief Terrance GAINER&#134;- talks about security & life-saving.]  [DC delegate Eleanor Holmes NORTON&nbsp- calls it seat-of-the-pants security.]", "segment_duration": 110, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63290.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761755, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "2inuCH7X9x", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761752, "segment_id": "EpebJy9K7Z", "segment_broadcast_id": "2inuCH7X9x", "segment_title": "Campaign 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry", "segment_description": "(Studio: Thalia Assuras)  Report introduced.   (La Junta, Colorado: Jim Axelrod)  The weekend whistle-stop campaigning by presidential candidate Senator John Kerry featured; scenes shown of the Kerry-Edwards train in Colorado & Missouri.  [From the train, in Missouri & in Colorado, KERRY&nbsp- campaigns.]", "segment_duration": 120, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63400.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761756, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "2inuCH7X9x", "broadcast_date": "2004-08-07", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcas